## Django REST Framework Guidelines

### Serializers

- Use DRF serializers for JSON responses and request validation
- Create separate serializers for different operations (create, update, read)
- Implement proper field validation and custom validators
- Use ModelSerializer for model-based serialization
- Handle nested serializers for complex data structures

### API Views

- Use ViewSets for CRUD operations on models
- Implement APIView for custom API behavior
- Use GenericAPIView for common patterns
- Implement proper pagination for list endpoints
- Use filters and search functionality

### Authentication & Permissions

- Use JWT authentication (djangorestframework-simplejwt)
- Implement proper permission classes
- Use IsAuthenticated for protected endpoints
- Implement custom permissions for business logic
- Handle token refresh and blacklisting

### API Documentation

- Use drf-spectacular for API documentation
- Write comprehensive docstrings for all endpoints
- Document request/response schemas
- Provide example requests and responses
- Use proper HTTP status codes

### Performance

- Optimize serializer performance with select_related/prefetch_related
- Implement caching for API responses
- Use pagination to limit response size
- Optimize database queries in serializers
